`minimum_network(node_count, links)` must compute a minimum-cost spanning network for nodes `0` through `node_count - 1`. Each link is `(left, right, cost)`. `node_count` must be a positive non-boolean integer. Endpoints must be valid non-boolean integers, and costs must be finite non-negative integers or floats, excluding booleans. Self-links may appear but cannot be selected. Parallel links are allowed.

Return `(matrix, selected, total)`. `matrix` is a symmetric adjacency matrix using `0` on its diagonal, the cheapest direct-link cost elsewhere, and `None` when absent. `selected` contains normalized `(smaller_endpoint, larger_endpoint, cost)` tuples in the deterministic Kruskal consideration order `(cost, smaller_endpoint, larger_endpoint)`. `total` is their sum. A one-node graph returns no selected links and total `0`. A disconnected graph raises `ValueError`. Do not mutate input links or alias any input container.

